  }

  /*
   * The disclosure holding the query, opting OUT of the site's `details` chrome.
   *
   * `details` is styled globally as a door — border, raised surface, padding, a
   * full-width hit area — because chapter 8 hides six evidence tables behind it
   * and a reviewer has to see that the proof is there. Inheriting that here was
   * wrong in a way worth recording: it rendered this panel as a bordered button,
   * which is the exact control that was removed from the site's navigation two
   * rounds ago for being ugly. The query is the thing the reader asked not to be
   * shown, so it has to read as a footnote, not as a door.
   *
   * Only the box is removed. The marker and its rotation stay inherited, so the
   * two kinds of disclosure on the site agree about which way a closed chevron
   * points — the first version of this block redefined `::before` and ended up
   * pointing right-then-down in chapter 8 and down-then-up here.
   */


  /* Also from the global rule: it draws a rule under an open summary to separate
     it from the table beneath. There is no frame here for that rule to close. */


  textarea {
    width: 100%;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.6;
    tab-size: 2;
    color: var(--text);
    background: var(--bg-sunken);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    resize: vertical;
  }
  textarea:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .status {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-faint);
    /* The figure face, not the terminal face. This line counts the rows in the
       table beside it, and its digits were in a different typeface from theirs. */
